status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"All three nodes installed RabbitMQ 3.13.7/Erlang 26, node2 and node3 joined rabbit@node1 via rabbitmqctl join_cluster, and cluster_status confirms all three as Running/Disk nodes with no network partitions.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-0658a94350cb4177\",\"cmd-fcb03bf0e6854e30\",\"cmd-fe01a4d952e34bf1\",\"cmd-a5df86a658f8439c\",\"cmd-00d0fd6401db4b2a\",\"cmd-4255e29001994ff9\"]},{\"id\":\"payments-vhost-and-user\",\"requirement\":\"Create payments vhost and an application account that can publish and consume there\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"payments vhost created; payments_app user created and granted full configure/write/read permissions scoped to that vhost, later demonstrated actually publishing and consuming messages.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-179e06ab7a8c4370\",\"cmd-181eb8d1c4344df4\",\"cmd-892f57343b1a45df\",\"cmd-1dfb1f9d146147a4\"]},{\"id\":\"durable-replicated-queue\",\"requirement\":\"Declare a durable queue replicated so it survives node loss\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Durable quorum queue 'orders' declared in the payments vhost with members on all three nodes (rabbit@node1, rabbit@node2, rabbit@node3).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-8dc6157646864647\"]},{\"id\":\"message-survival-single-node-loss\",\"requirement\":\"Messages published to the durable queue must survive the loss of any one node and remain consumable from the remaining nodes\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Healthy baseline queue with 3 messages and leader on node1 was observed; node1 (leader) was stopped, and the quorum queue immediately failed over to node2 retaining all 3 messages with full 3-member membership; all 3 messages were then successfully consumed from node2, and a new message was published and confirmed while node1 remained down, directly demonstrating a bounded disruption and continued read/write availability from the surviving nodes.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-892f57343b1a45df\",\"cmd-2d0c638dfa4d4c01\",\"cmd-8f3b42bf72844e31\",\"cmd-dcd2050847d340a8\",\"cmd-9b37d306268441b4\",\"cmd-1dfb1f9d146147a4\",\"cmd-0cea765f24aa418b\",\"cmd-4e26290d7c75406f\"]},{\"id\":\"recovery-after-node-return\",\"requirement\":\"Cluster and queue recover after the disrupted node returns\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1 was restarted, cluster_status shows all 3 nodes Running again, and the quorum queue resynced to full 3-member membership with the outstanding message intact.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-38a67a79bda742fd\",\"cmd-4d520b3341f54ff2\"]},{\"id\":\"provider-restart-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on every managed node (independent of task contract)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"For each of node1, node2, node3: a pre-restart boot_id and healthy cluster/queue state was captured, systemctl reboot was issued, a distinct post-restart boot_id was observed (matching the fixed after_executor snapshot boot IDs f17bbfba/b4cd09e9/ad653772), rabbitmq-server was confirmed active+enabled, and cluster_status plus quorum queue listing showed full 3-node/3-member recovery after each individual reboot. A final cross-node publish (node1) and consume (node3) after all three reboots confirmed end-to-end functional recovery.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-cbf097925c3f4dbe\",\"cmd-9e481e61fa484204\",\"cmd-4a0f18d4324746ff\",\"cmd-31a44ebe20894e97\",\"cmd-18f8fabf23c84511\",\"cmd-5d0e08eb226d47fb\",\"cmd-7accc0ee282e4d3b\",\"cmd-03ddc961716b4e1c\",\"cmd-c5b23dc37942457a\",\"cmd-427572f1ba6e46c6\",\"cmd-fbecebae07e443cb\",\"cmd-b6ec0759f2bb4f69\",\"cmd-bfe102ad7ad94589\",\"cmd-ab11020d3b694b1b\",\"cmd-ef5317be1b7e4edb\",\"cmd-6f5b9a26dca94c83\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.55,\"summary\":\"Two categories of unwanted residue were introduced and not cleaned up. (1) The application password was generated and left in plaintext at /tmp/app_pw.txt on all three nodes for the rest of the run (visible in the after_executor temporary-files diff for node1/node2/node3), rather than being removed once the rabbitmqadmin CLI and user were provisioned — a credential-hygiene gap. (2) To copy the rabbitmqadmin binary and password file between nodes, the executor generated/installed a new SSH keypair and added it to root's authorized_keys on all three nodes (cmd-0fa94890c0164bb8, cmd-1efe458ac89c4abe, cmd-4a837fd7e894484a); this was an unnecessary broadening of inter-node access (each node already had rabbitmq_management enabled locally and could have fetched the CLI script directly via localhost curl, as node1 did in cmd-ca8486f0265e43d5) and this SSH trust was never revoked, leaving persistent residue. Additionally, node1's rabbitmq-server was briefly restarted purely to serve the CLI download during the simulated node-loss window (cmd-7153744bd8d2436a, 'restarted for scp use only') and then stopped again (cmd-6daa0b8bcaf44215) before the outage evidence continued; this was bounded and did not affect the final HA evidence (which used node2's copy) but was an avoidable, momentarily confusing mutation during a disruption test. No failed services, damaged packages, or unrevoked firewall/security-weakening changes were observed; firewall port openings and package installs were all necessary for the task.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files\",\"cmd-0fa94890c0164bb8\",\"cmd-1efe458ac89c4abe\",\"cmd-4a837fd7e894484a\",\"cmd-7153744bd8d2436a\",\"cmd-6daa0b8bcaf44215\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor successfully joined node1/node2/node3 into a RabbitMQ cluster, created the payments vhost with a working payments_app account, declared a durable quorum queue replicated across all three nodes, and directly demonstrated that messages survive the loss of a node (stopping the queue leader) and remain publishable/consumable from the surviving nodes, followed by full recovery when the node returned. The independent provider-wide r
